  <content>
  <section><title><span>Warm Up Activity</span></title>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Study the table. What do you notice? What do you wonder?</para>
    <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
      <thead/>
      <tbody>
        <row>
          <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
            \(x\)
          </entry>
          <entry>
            0
          </entry>
          <entry>
            1
          </entry>
          <entry>
            2
          </entry>
          <entry>
            3
          </entry>
          <entry>
            4
          </entry>
          <entry>
            5
          </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
            \(y\)
          </entry>
          <entry>
            0
          </entry>
          <entry>
            16
          </entry>
          <entry>
            64
          </entry>
          <entry>
            144
          </entry>
          <entry>
            256
          </entry>
          <entry>
            400
          </entry>
        </row>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    
  </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Things you may notice:</para>
    <list>
      <item> The \(x\)-values increment by 1 as you move across the table. </item>
      <item> The \(y\)-values increase. </item>
      <item> All \(y\)-values are even and divisible by 4, 8, and 16. </item>
      <item> The \(y\)-values are all perfect squares. </item>
      <item> The successive differences between the \(y\)-values are growing. </item>
    </list>
    <para>Things you may wonder:</para>
    <list>
      <item> Is there a rule for these numbers? </item>
      <item> Do the numbers represent the growth of a geometric pattern? </item>
      <item> Do the numbers represent a quadratic relationship? </item>
      <item> What is the next number in the table?</item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
